General_SiSo_Auto_REC_RU_safe_mode_improper_voltage_input
    [Documentation]    Purpose of this test case is to check if RMOD enters safe mode when improper voltage is applied.
    ...                Voltage thresholds are defined by alVoltLowThreshold and alVoltHighThreshold parameters.
    ...                Fault ID: 2920 EFaultId_RfLowVoltageAl should appear on RMOD when voltage is too low;
    ...                Fault ID: 2919 EFaultId_RfHighVoltageAl should appear on RMOD when voltage is too high;
    ...                Fault ID: 4680 EFaultId_RfUnstableVoltageAI should appear when above faults appear number of times
    ...                defined by alVoltUnstableThreshold parameter.
    ...                ARGS:
    ...                - ${rmod_id} - configuration ID of RMOD to be tested i.e. 1, 2, 3, etc.
    ...                - ${too_low_voltage} - value of voltage that will trigger fault 2920; defaults to 40000mV
    ...                - ${too_high_voltage} - value of voltage that will trigger fault 2919; defaults to 58000mV
    ...                - ${throughputs} - dict with throughput and deviation values for each cell identified by
    ...                             it's nrCellIdentity for NR cells, eutranCellId for LTE cells, wnCelId for WCDMA cells.
    ...                             Example:
    ...                             {
    ...                                 '827736065':
    ...                                      {
    ...                                          'throughput':
    ...                                              {
    ...                                                  'downlink': '100 Mbits/sec',
    ...                                                  'uplink': '15 Mbits/sec'
    ...                                              },
    ...                                          'deviation': '90%'
    ...                                      },
    ...                             }; defaults to None (L3 Call will not be executed)
    ...              - ${protocol} - data transfer protocol; defaults to UDP.
    ...              - ${udp_buffer} - monitoring data buffer; defaults to 4M.
    ...              - ${tput_verification_via_btslog} - True - throughput verification will be performed using btslog
    ...                                                  False - throughput verification will be performed using iperf; defaults to False
    ...              - ${ue_network_modes} - dict with UE serial numbers and desired network modes e.g. {"SN1234": "NR_only"}
    ...                                  possible UE network modes: NR_only, LTE_only, NR_LTE
    ...                                  when using more than one UE please make sure that the modes you choose are either all
    ...                                  with "_only" suffix or all "NR_LTE" as it is not yet possible to mix those.
    ...                                  mandatory for SA+NSA setups, defaults to None
    ...              - ${ignored_cells_on_preparation} - SHOULD BE USED WITH `prepare_cells_to_call` set to True!
    ...                                                  list of cells CONFIGURATION distnames that should be ignored during
    ...                                                  L3 Call not called cells preparation procedure and not be blocked/barred
    ...              - ${switch_to_rfsw_user} - True if user wants to switch to 'rfsw' user after connection to RMOD,
    ...                                         False if user wants to stay with 'serviceuser' user;
    ...                                         defaults to True.
    ...              - ${fault_id_to_trigger_4680} - fault ID that will be used to trigger unstable voltage alarm (4680);
    ...                                              defaults to 2919 (high voltage fault).
